%[text] Implement the Crank-Nicolson method that uses a trapezoidal integral approximation. This is equivalent to the average of the [explicit method $(\\mathcal{E})${"altText":"(E)"}](internal:M_89C3E8C8) and the [implicit method $(\\mathcal{I})${"altText":"(I)"}](internal:M_56AE4F3A), literally $\\frac{(\\mathcal{E})+(\\mathcal{I})}{2}${"altText":"((E)+(I))\/(2)"}.
